sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: a synchronous read of the Metrics role through Grafana; no run, no stored sample. docs/reference/metrics.md#read-node-metrics.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:metrics
  %% kind: node.metrics
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane M icon=server pill=observer tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant M as Metrics<br/>Grafana · Prom.
  CLI->>GW: node:metrics NODE
  %% path: main
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:metrics NODE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node>`
  Note over GW: Validate the read
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the Node exists (`http.404`), and the calling Node has an access grant to it (`node_access.required`)
  %%> - the target is active and has a WireGuard address (`node.metrics_unavailable`)
  %%> - exactly one Node holds the Metrics role; it is active and has stored credentials (`metrics.assignment_missing`, `metrics.assignment_drift`, `metrics.node_inactive`, `metrics.credentials_missing`)
  %%> Why no run:
  %%> - this is a synchronous read through Grafana, not a read of Gateway-recorded metrics; it changes no Node and stores no sample
  alt read refused
    %% path: refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>error_code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - returns the matching requirement's error before querying Grafana; nothing is changed
  else read admitted
    %% path: read-admitted
    GW->>M: Read exporter snapshot<br/>four metric-group queries
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - discovers the Prometheus datasource through Grafana and queries the target's exporter with the stored credential
    %%> - one query reads memory, swap, load and uptime; one each reads cores, pressure and disks
    %%> - only the first query decides whether a snapshot exists; it must contain total-memory samples
    M-->>GW: Samples or query failure
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a failed datasource lookup or required query fails the read; each optional query can fail independently
    alt required read fails
      %% path: unreachable
      GW--xCLI: 502 Bad Gateway<br/>node.metrics_unreachable
      %%> Result:
      %%> - a required-query failure or absent total-memory sample returns no partial snapshot; nothing is stored or changed
    else scalar sample exists
      %% path: sampled
      Note over GW: Build the snapshot
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - excludes pseudo filesystems such as `tmpfs` and `proc`; sorts `/` first and other mounts by name
      %%> - orders cores by index; missing pressure values are `0`
      opt an optional query fails
        %% path: optional-failure
        Note over GW: Keep available groups
        %%> Result:
        %%> - failed cores or disks queries produce empty lists; a failed pressure query uses the missing-pressure default
      end
      GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>one snapshot
      %% path: succeeded
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the Node's name and ID with cores, memory, swap, load, uptime, pressure and disks
      %%> Repeat:
      %%> - reads again after success or failure; this is not an already-applied skip and has no skip reason code
    end
  end
